From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] io/fileview: hear a directory's files with one watch

A FileView watching a directory never said it changed. Its path was
watched as a directory, never as a file, and a change in a directory was
taken only as news that the file named had just been made. So a shell
hearing a folder of files held a FileView, and an open watch, for every
file in it: 406 of them took one shell near its limit of open files, and
a start's burst went past it.

A FileView whose path names a directory now says it changed whenever a
file in it is made, renamed in or out, or removed, with the one watch.
It keeps that watch as the nearest directory above it is watched, and is
heard once it's made, as a file is. A FileView of a file hears what it
heard before.

---
diff --git a/src/io/fileview.cpp b/src/io/fileview.cpp
index 59409a4..bd9fb1a 100644
--- a/src/io/fileview.cpp
+++ b/src/io/fileview.cpp
@@ -566,12 +566,15 @@ void FileView::watchNearest() {
 	}
 
 	for (const auto& watched: this->watcher->directories()) {
-		if (watched != dirPath) this->watcher->removePath(watched);
+		if (watched != dirPath && watched != this->targetPath) this->watcher->removePath(watched);
 	}
 
 	if (!this->watcher->directories().contains(dirPath)) this->watcher->addPath(dirPath);
 
-	if (!this->watcher->files().contains(this->targetPath) && QFileInfo::exists(this->targetPath)) {
+	// A directory is watched as one, so it's heard as anything in it changes.
+	const auto& watched =
+	    QFileInfo(this->targetPath).isDir() ? this->watcher->directories() : this->watcher->files();
+	if (!watched.contains(this->targetPath) && QFileInfo::exists(this->targetPath)) {
 		this->watcher->addPath(this->targetPath);
 	}
 }
@@ -584,12 +587,23 @@ void FileView::onWatchedFileChanged() {
 	emit this->fileChanged();
 }
 
-void FileView::onWatchedDirectoryChanged() {
-	auto wasWatched = this->watcher->files().contains(this->targetPath);
+void FileView::onWatchedDirectoryChanged(const QString& path) {
+	auto watching = [this] {
+		return this->watcher->files().contains(this->targetPath)
+		    || this->watcher->directories().contains(this->targetPath);
+	};
+
+	auto wasWatched = watching();
 	this->watchNearest();
 
+	// a directory's own change is its content's: a file made, renamed in or removed
+	if (path == this->targetPath) {
+		emit this->fileChanged();
+		return;
+	}
+
 	// the file was just created, perhaps with the directories above it
-	if (!wasWatched && this->watcher->files().contains(this->targetPath)) emit this->fileChanged();
+	if (!wasWatched && watching()) emit this->fileChanged();
 }
 
 bool FileView::shouldBlockRead() const {
diff --git a/src/io/fileview.hpp b/src/io/fileview.hpp
index 1f62f2f..3e16c1c 100644
--- a/src/io/fileview.hpp
+++ b/src/io/fileview.hpp
@@ -211,7 +211,8 @@ class FileView: public QObject {
 	/// If true (defaule false), @@fileChanged() will be called whenever the content of the file
 	/// changes on disk, including when @@setText() or @@setData() are used. A file that does not
 	/// exist yet, or whose directory does not, is heard once it is made, and again if its
-	/// directory is removed and made again.
+	/// directory is removed and made again. A path naming a directory is heard whenever a file in
+	/// it is made, renamed in or out, or removed, with one watch for the whole directory.
 	///
 	/// > [!NOTE] You can reload the file's content whenever it changes on disk like so:
 	/// > ```qml
@@ -380,7 +381,7 @@ private:
 	void updateWatchedFiles();
 	void watchNearest();
 	void onWatchedFileChanged();
-	void onWatchedDirectoryChanged();
+	void onWatchedDirectoryChanged(const QString& path);
 
 	[[nodiscard]] bool shouldBlockRead() const;
 	[[nodiscard]] FileViewReader* liveReader() const;
